# Day 005 – Hero Reset

## Date

03 August 2026

---

## What I Did Today

Today was supposed to be the day I finally started building the new Hero.

I spent some time working with the current layout, but the more I changed it, the more I realized it didn't match the vision I had in my head.

At one point, I even deleted around 220 lines of code because I thought starting from scratch would be easier.

Thankfully, I immediately hit **Ctrl + Z**, and everything came back. Nothing was actually lost.

Instead of forcing myself to keep coding, I decided to stop and rethink the architecture before making any more changes.

---

## Hero

Today wasn't really about writing code—it was about planning the experience.

After reviewing the current Hero, I realized the problem wasn't the code itself. The user experience had changed, and trying to keep modifying the existing layout was only making things more confusing.

I now have a much clearer plan.

The landing page will begin with only the Hero content visible.

As the user scrolls, the Hero text will smoothly shrink and move to the left while the product showcase appears on the right.

Instead of rebuilding everything from scratch, I'll reorganize the Hero into smaller, focused components and build the layout first.

Once the layout closely matches my design, I'll move on to implementing the scroll animation, automatic card rotation, dashboard switching, and finally polish everything with smooth animations.

I also decided to follow a simple development philosophy throughout the project:

> **Don't optimize early. First make it work, then make it beautiful, then make it reusable.**

